      "description": "Summit Ridge Energy develops, constructs, owns, and operates distributed solar and battery-storage systems across the U.S. Midwest, Mid-Atlantic, and New England. Founded in 2017, the company reported more than 275 facilities and over 3 GW of operating and development-stage solar and storage projects in July 2026. Apollo-managed funds made a $175 million strategic platform investment in 2022; the exact Apollo stake, fund and legal vehicle are not publicly disclosed. On July 14, 2026, Global Infrastructure Partners, a part of BlackRock, agreed through its mid-market infrastructure strategy to acquire a majority and controlling interest, subject to customary closing conditions and regulatory approvals. No closing announcement was identified through August 12, 2026, so Apollo remains the current legal owner and GIP is recorded only as a signed pending counterparty. Apollo's separate 2025 commitment of up to $400 million relates to an Illinois solar-asset joint venture rather than a second corporate ownership period.",
